<title>USA: Turner declines comment on layoffs.</title>
<headline>Turner declines comment on layoffs.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turner Broadcasting System Inc declined comment on Wednesday on a newpaper report saying the company would shed no more than 500 jobs in its merger with Time Warner Inc.</p>
<p>The Atlanta Journal-Constitution quoted TBS executive vice president Terence McGuirk as saying of the possible layoff count: &quot;I'd be surprised if it were 500.&quot; He also said the company still planned to shave expenses by $100 million.</p>
<p>&quot;We have no comment,&quot; a TBS spokesman said.</p>
</text>
